            <ArticleTitle>What can be done to meet the needs of older people experiencing pain?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is a myth that older people feel pain less than younger people. They may have more difficulty communicating what they are experiencing, and health-care practitioners need to be aware of different ways of monitoring this. Obstacles include outdated attitudes, the underuse of opioids, and ineffective use of pain measurement scales.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
